From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 17:03:53 +0000
Subject: libcamera: delayed_controls: Read not yet queued frames as the latest
 values

get() indexes the history by sequence number, and returns whatever sits
in the ring slot for a frame whose controls have not been queued yet: an
empty ControlValue before the ring has wrapped, stale values after. That
happens whenever the IPA falls behind the frames, as the pipeline then
asks for the controls of a frame before the IPA has pushed any for it.
The soft IPA reads them with ControlValue::get<int32_t>(), which asserts
on an empty value in debug builds and returns garbage otherwise.

Nothing has changed the controls since the most recently queued values,
so return those.

Signed-off-by: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
---
 src/libcamera/delayed_controls.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/delayed_controls.cpp b/src/libcamera/delayed_controls.cpp
index 5b3ced4e7..2a291fefb 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/delayed_controls.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/delayed_controls.cpp
@@ -198,12 +198,19 @@ bool DelayedControls::push(const ControlList &controls)
  * push(). The max history from the current sequence number that yields valid
  * values are thus 16 minus number of controls pushed.
  *
+ * A sequence number for which no controls have been queued yet, as happens
+ * when the IPA falls behind the frames, reads the most recently queued values:
+ * nothing has changed them since.
+ *
  * \return The controls at \a sequence number
  */
 ControlList DelayedControls::get(uint32_t sequence)
 {
 	unsigned int index = std::max<int>(0, sequence - maxDelay_);
 
+	if (index >= queueCount_)
+		index = queueCount_ - 1;
+
